{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_y5t5xmp3olgkpo3uucryn42bnqwr7mfglic35eyuuo62o23bh4aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases are complete and verified.\n\n## Phase A — both build\n- **C:** `cmake -S c_src -B c_src/build && cmake --build c_src/build` → `c_src/build/driver ARG1 ARG2`\n- **Rust:** `cd translation && cargo build --release` → `translation/target/release/driver ARG1 ARG2`\n\nBoth compiled with zero errors; no source changes were needed to `translation/src/main.rs`.\n\n## Phase B/C — differential tests\n`translation/tests/differential.rs` (31 tests) spawns **both binaries** as subprocesses with identical `argv` and asserts stdout, stderr *and* exit status. The C program is built by the test itself via CMake into `translation/target/c_build`, so `c_src/` is never written to by the suite.\n\nInput classes derived from reading the C, all covered:\n- `argc != 3` (0, 1, 3, 5 args) → error + exit 1\n- `end == argv[1]` and `end == argv[2]` error paths (`\"\"`, `abc`, whitespace-only, bare `-`/`+`, `0x`, non-UTF-8 bytes), including that argv[1] is validated *first*\n- `iterations <= 0` (empty output, exit 0), single iteration\n- both `static_alias` branches (`*outer >= inner` and `*outer < inner`) and the switch-over point\n- `int` overflow of the doubling `inner`, `long`→`int` truncation, `strtol` saturation to `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN`, base-10-only parsing, trailing junk, `isspace()` including `\\v`/`\\f`\n- sweeps: full grid `[-20,20] × [0,12]`, `int`-extremes table, 650 deterministic pseudorandom cases\n\n## Result\n**No mismatches.** `cargo test` → 31/31 passing, and `cargo test --release` → 31/31 (checked separately because a non-wrapping `+` would panic only in debug). The C was also rebuilt with `-O3` and still matched, confirming the overflow modelling. Nothing is `#[ignore]`d or skipped, and `c_src/` sources are byte-identical to the originals.\n\n`translation/ERRORS.md` records the full branch-to-test map plus the ten behaviours that had to be preserved and how each was verified — notably that the C prints its errors to **stdout** (`printf`, not stderr) while exiting 1, that `strtol` accepts `12abc`/`+7`/`0x10`-as-0 where `str::parse` would not, and that out-of-range input saturates to `LONG_MAX` and *then* truncates to `-1`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1247,"cache_read_input_tokens":43242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"576b6ddd-b1cf-4f8c-a53a-cf0394a630f2","uuid":"ee85c81a-29c2-408e-8b70-12e7ea5eb804","timestamp":"2026-08-28T10:01:03.438Z"}
